Z||000002||Steve Normington||06-12-2001||11:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by dr fritz:<BR><B>when converting 2.8 to 3.1... are the same intake manifolds used? is their a better aftermarket intake manifold to use?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Use the same intake manifold as the stock.<P>You can also use the stock injectors. You might want to get an adjustable fuel pressure regulator so that you can tweak it.<P>Sorry, that is the sum total of my knowledge.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||06-12-2001||11:58 AM||||--are the same intake manifolds used? <P>yes<P>--is their a better aftermarket intake manifold to use?<P>West Coast Fiero's has a sweet new prototype...<P>--also is the 2.8 wrist pin compatible to the 3.1 rod? <P>nope, you can use the same 2.8 rods, but the pistons have a higher wrist pin location.<P>--can anyone recommend the best piston for the buck?<P>Mine weren't too expencive, I don't have my bill sheet in front of me though, I'll try to remember to post them tonight.<P>--what type of injector will work best for this application?<P>stock... I haven't had any problems with mine, make sure you clean them and replace the o-rings.<P>--has anyone played around with the throttle body diameter?<P>check out Chris West's prototype intake, or get one of the big bore ones from the fiero store. I myself am still running stock intake, 3.1 crank .040 bore, ported exhaust manifolds, cat eliminator and ocealot exhaust. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||06-12-2001||02:32 PM||||If you're going to bore out the t-body then it's best to have the upper plenum done at the same time. Darrel Morse did mine and only charges $150.00 for the whole job.<BR>(that even includes return shipping)<P>Darrels email: morse86@aol.com<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
